What this does:

- Keeps the visual “drop‐here” button (`<div role="button">…</div>`) entirely separate from the native `<input>`.
- The `<input>` remains immediately after, still inside the `<label>` so that clicks/keyboard events bubble correctly.
- Because the focusable `<input>` is no longer a descendant of the element with `role="button"`, axe will no longer flag a nested‐interactive violation.
